// BetaUpload.xcconfig.example — TEMPLATE. This file IS committed; the real
// BetaUpload.xcconfig is gitignored so the beta token never enters git history.
//
// Setup:
//   cp BetaUpload.xcconfig.example BetaUpload.xcconfig
// then fill in both values from the CloudFormation stack outputs:
//   aws cloudformation describe-stacks --region us-east-1 \
//     --stack-name loftmeter-beta-diag --query 'Stacks[0].Outputs' --output table
//
// BetaUploadAPIBase — the stack's ApiEndpoint output. The client appends /presign.
// BetaUploadToken   — the BetaUploadToken parameter the stack was deployed with.
//                     It is the X-Beta-Key abuse gate, not real auth.
//
// These reach the app through MotoTelemetryApp/Info.plist, which references them as
// $(BetaUploadAPIBase) / $(BetaUploadToken). Do NOT try to set them as
// INFOPLIST_KEY_BetaUploadAPIBase build settings instead: Xcode's INFOPLIST_KEY_
// prefix only honours Info.plist keys Apple defines and silently drops custom ones.
//
// Attached as the app target's DEBUG baseConfigurationReference only. Release gets
// neither value, and the uploader is behind #if BETA regardless.
//
// NOTE the SLASH indirection. In an .xcconfig file `//` begins a comment, so writing
// the URL literally truncates the value to `https:` with no warning.

SLASH = /

BetaUploadAPIBase = https:$(SLASH)$(SLASH)REPLACE-WITH-ApiEndpoint-HOST
BetaUploadToken = REPLACE_WITH_BETA_TOKEN
